1
00:00:01,827 --> 00:00:04,569
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

2
00:01:31,569 --> 00:01:34,703
[whimsical music]
[crowd chattering]

3
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:36,183
- [Hiraku] Today we're
all enjoying

4
00:01:36,313 --> 00:01:38,402
another peaceful morning.

5
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:42,102
The Great Tree Village has
become quite lively lately.

6
00:01:43,146 --> 00:01:44,974
[Hiraku groans]

7
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:46,671
My day starts once the sun

8
00:01:46,802 --> 00:01:48,891
has completely risen
each morning.

9
00:01:49,021 --> 00:01:50,849
That's when I wake up.

10
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:51,850
[Hiraku sighs]

11
00:01:51,981 --> 00:01:53,069
- [Lu] Good morning.

12
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,114
- Huh?

13
00:01:54,244 --> 00:01:56,072
Hey, good morning.

14
00:01:56,203 --> 00:01:57,769
Are you feeling all right?

15
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,859
- Geez, you ask me that
every time you see me.

16
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:02,557
- Oh, I didn't realize,

17
00:02:02,687 --> 00:02:05,342
but I'm sure things
are tough for you.

18
00:02:05,473 --> 00:02:07,736
Once we found out
that Lu was pregnant,

19
00:02:07,866 --> 00:02:10,869
the entire village went
into a joyous uproar.

20
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,046
- So that's how come I haven't
been able to transform.

21
00:02:14,177 --> 00:02:16,005
- [Hiraku] Is that how it works?

22
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,486
She was the most calm
out of everyone.

23
00:02:18,616 --> 00:02:21,228
- You don't need to worry
so much about me, Hiraku.

24
00:02:21,358 --> 00:02:24,187
I'm sure everything
will be fine.

25
00:02:24,318 --> 00:02:26,146
- [sighs] You sure?

26
00:02:26,276 --> 00:02:29,975
- Yeah, I'm going to go check
on the medicinal herb garden.

27
00:02:30,106 --> 00:02:32,021
- [Hiraku] Mm-hmm, are you
fine by yourself?

28
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,675
- [Lu] You are doing it again.

29
00:02:33,805 --> 00:02:34,763
- [Hiraku] Ah, sorry.

30
00:02:34,893 --> 00:02:36,243
[Lu giggles]

31
00:02:36,373 --> 00:02:38,723
Now back to my morning schedule.

32
00:02:38,854 --> 00:02:40,334
According to Anne and the maids,

33
00:02:40,464 --> 00:02:43,206
it's my job to keep an eye on
things around the house.

34
00:02:43,337 --> 00:02:44,903
- Hello, good morning.

35
00:02:45,034 --> 00:02:46,557
- Hey, morning.

36
00:02:46,688 --> 00:02:48,342
By the way, there's a reason

37
00:02:48,472 --> 00:02:51,345
I don't wake up too early
in the morning.

38
00:02:51,475 --> 00:02:53,260
Anne and the other maids
all insist

39
00:02:53,390 --> 00:02:56,001
on waking up
earlier than I do.

40
00:02:56,132 --> 00:02:58,830
I sleep later
for their sakes.

41
00:02:58,961 --> 00:03:01,093
I'm definitely not being lazy.

42
00:03:01,224 --> 00:03:02,704
When I see her in the morning,

43
00:03:02,834 --> 00:03:05,228
she lets me know if she
has anything to report.

44
00:03:05,359 --> 00:03:06,664
- [Anne] Last night,
the wine slime

45
00:03:06,795 --> 00:03:08,231
snuck into the
food storage area,

46
00:03:08,362 --> 00:03:10,233
and drank an entire
barrel of wine.

47
00:03:10,364 --> 00:03:11,843
- [Hiraku] Was that
the one we left out

48
00:03:11,974 --> 00:03:13,541
to keep the wine slime
from the rest?

49
00:03:13,671 --> 00:03:14,977
- [Anne] Yes, I'm not sure

50
00:03:15,107 --> 00:03:16,587
if we should celebrate
our plan working,

51
00:03:16,718 --> 00:03:18,328
or if we should
be lamenting the fact

52
00:03:18,459 --> 00:03:20,243
that we let it
sneak in at all.

53
00:03:20,374 --> 00:03:22,463
- [Hiraku] Let's just say
it went according to plan.

54
00:03:22,593 --> 00:03:24,856
Once I make my rounds
around the house,

55
00:03:24,987 --> 00:03:26,336
it's time for breakfast.

56
00:03:26,467 --> 00:03:28,338
We can't fit everyone in
the dining hall at once,

57
00:03:28,469 --> 00:03:30,297
so we split breakfast
into three groups.

58
00:03:30,427 --> 00:03:32,473
- For today's main
breakfast menu,

59
00:03:32,603 --> 00:03:35,432
we have a soup of daikon radish,
spinach, and cabbage,

60
00:03:35,563 --> 00:03:38,130
and smoked killer rabbit
seared to perfection.

61
00:03:38,261 --> 00:03:39,828
- Wow. Sounds delicious.

62
00:03:39,958 --> 00:03:41,699
It looks great... hmm, Flora?

63
00:03:41,830 --> 00:03:43,962
- One microorganism,
two microorganisms.

64
00:03:44,093 --> 00:03:46,400
- [Hiraku] Have you
not been sleeping?

65
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:48,924
- I haven't made any
progress on the miso.

66
00:03:49,054 --> 00:03:51,100
- [Hiraku] This is about
20% of the way there.

67
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:54,234
- [screams] It's because
you say stuff like that.

68
00:03:54,364 --> 00:03:56,584
I'm sure I just need
more of this stuff.

69
00:03:56,714 --> 00:03:59,151
- [Hiraku] I apologize, I
implore you, get some sleep.

70
00:03:59,282 --> 00:04:02,807
The second breakfast group
is the maids.

71
00:04:02,938 --> 00:04:05,245
Then the third group is
whoever didn't make it in time

72
00:04:05,375 --> 00:04:07,029
for the first or second groups.

73
00:04:07,159 --> 00:04:09,161
Sometimes Hakuren
doesn't even make it

74
00:04:09,292 --> 00:04:11,033
in time for the third group.

75
00:04:11,163 --> 00:04:12,339
[Hakuren snoring]

76
00:04:12,469 --> 00:04:14,993
- I'm here to make a report.

77
00:04:15,124 --> 00:04:16,647
- [Hiraku] Did something happen?

78
00:04:16,778 --> 00:04:18,736
- [Granmaria] Yesterday, a
group of three killer rabbits

79
00:04:18,867 --> 00:04:21,173
attempted to infiltrate
the village.

80
00:04:21,304 --> 00:04:23,132
Kuro and the dogs
eliminated them.

81
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:25,569
- [Hiraku] I see, those rabbits
never learn their lesson.

82
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,963
- Well, we're able to
use them as food,

83
00:04:28,093 --> 00:04:31,662
so we should be thankful
they act the way they do.

84
00:04:31,793 --> 00:04:32,837
- [Hiraku] Good point.

85
00:04:32,968 --> 00:04:34,404
You know?
- [Granmaria] Hmm?

86
00:04:34,535 --> 00:04:36,232
- Even though Granmaria
and the other angels

87
00:04:36,363 --> 00:04:38,365
always seem so composed
and proper,

88
00:04:38,495 --> 00:04:40,062
they all enter lazy mode

89
00:04:40,192 --> 00:04:42,282
when they're off duty
and on their own time.

90
00:04:42,412 --> 00:04:44,022
They can't really do any chores,

91
00:04:44,153 --> 00:04:46,677
so Anne and the maids
prepare their food,

92
00:04:46,808 --> 00:04:48,766
while they rely on Daga
and the other lizardmen

93
00:04:48,897 --> 00:04:51,073
to do their laundry
and other cleaning.

94
00:04:51,203 --> 00:04:52,901
Well, they do make up for it

95
00:04:53,031 --> 00:04:55,338
with how hard they work
to keep the village safe.

96
00:04:55,469 --> 00:04:57,906
I'm glad we have them here.
- [Granmaria] Hmm?

97
00:04:58,646 --> 00:05:00,778
- Hey, good morning.

98
00:05:02,824 --> 00:05:06,175
Once I've eaten, it's time to
move on to working the fields.

99
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:08,395
Huh, these things again?

100
00:05:08,525 --> 00:05:10,962
None of the normal garden
pests I'm familiar with

101
00:05:11,093 --> 00:05:12,790
exist in this world,

102
00:05:12,921 --> 00:05:15,837
but instead we have these
weird little black things

103
00:05:15,967 --> 00:05:18,100
that live on the plants
and eat their leaves.

104
00:05:18,230 --> 00:05:22,060
Fortunately, Zabuton's kids
or Kuro and the other dogs

105
00:05:22,191 --> 00:05:23,584
can spot them for us.

106
00:05:23,714 --> 00:05:26,630
As of now, they've yet
to cause any real damage.

107
00:05:26,761 --> 00:05:29,154
And the way I deal with them is-
[pests screaming]

108
00:05:29,285 --> 00:05:32,288
Using the almighty farming
tool as a watering can.

109
00:05:32,419 --> 00:05:35,509
Apparently it has the power
to eliminate garden pests.

110
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:37,989
The fields that we've
been slowly expanding

111
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:40,122
have become quite large in size.

112
00:05:40,252 --> 00:05:42,646
Checking on all of them
is pretty tough now.

113
00:05:42,777 --> 00:05:46,476
But seeing all the matured
crops fills me with joy,

114
00:05:46,607 --> 00:05:48,130
and with a sense of satisfaction

115
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:51,089
for all the work we've done
[sighs].

116
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:55,355
While I'm working on my chores,
lunch time comes around.

117
00:05:55,485 --> 00:05:57,226
I eat the lunch that
Anne and the maids

118
00:05:57,357 --> 00:06:00,403
prepare in between
my work. [moaning]

119
00:06:00,534 --> 00:06:01,970
[girls giggling]

120
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,146
Apparently having lunch
in this world

121
00:06:04,276 --> 00:06:06,191
is very out of the ordinary.

122
00:06:06,322 --> 00:06:08,237
- A meal in the afternoon?

123
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:10,282
But we just had a big meal
this morning.

124
00:06:10,413 --> 00:06:13,764
- I felt the very same way
when I first came here.

125
00:06:13,895 --> 00:06:16,158
- [Hiraku] Lunch aside,
Lea and the high elves

126
00:06:16,288 --> 00:06:18,290
were nervous about
even eating breakfast.

127
00:06:18,421 --> 00:06:19,988
- [Lea] Is it okay
if we eat today too?

128
00:06:20,118 --> 00:06:22,382
Will our food reserves
hold out at this rate?

129
00:06:22,512 --> 00:06:23,992
- [Hiraku] According to them,

130
00:06:24,122 --> 00:06:26,211
sometimes they went without
eating even a single meal.

131
00:06:26,342 --> 00:06:28,257
- You mean we get to eat food
every single day?

132
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:30,215
We're definitely going to
get kicked out

133
00:06:30,346 --> 00:06:32,261
of this village one day,
aren't we?

134
00:06:32,392 --> 00:06:34,350
- [Hiraku] How did she
reach that conclusion?

135
00:06:34,481 --> 00:06:36,787
I want to make sure that
none of them have to worry

136
00:06:36,918 --> 00:06:39,311
about food as long as
they're living here.

137
00:06:39,442 --> 00:06:40,661
- Excuse me, Mayor.

138
00:06:40,791 --> 00:06:41,923
- [Hiraku] Hmm?

139
00:06:42,053 --> 00:06:43,794
- The cows gave birth
to their calves.

140
00:06:43,925 --> 00:06:46,362
I would like to increase
their allotted feed.

141
00:06:46,493 --> 00:06:48,059
- Yeah, do that.

142
00:06:48,190 --> 00:06:51,411
- Hiraku, our crop storage room
is going to be full soon.

143
00:06:51,541 --> 00:06:52,977
- Shall we bring Michael here,

144
00:06:53,108 --> 00:06:55,371
and talk about selling
more of what we produce?

145
00:06:55,502 --> 00:06:58,156
- Yeah, talk to Flowrem
on quantity.

146
00:06:58,809 --> 00:07:00,463
[Hiraku groans]

147
00:07:00,594 --> 00:07:03,814
After lunchtime ends,
it's back to work.

148
00:07:05,381 --> 00:07:06,687
Having more people around

149
00:07:06,817 --> 00:07:09,254
has helped with the
farm work a lot, hmm?

150
00:07:09,385 --> 00:07:11,039
[dog whimpering]

151
00:07:11,169 --> 00:07:13,911
But tilling new fields
or planting new crops

152
00:07:14,042 --> 00:07:17,828
is something I handle myself
with the almighty farming tool.

153
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:19,874
[Hiraku grunts]

154
00:07:20,004 --> 00:07:21,658
[mysterious music]

155
00:07:21,789 --> 00:07:24,313
Up until now, I've only been
growing stuff we could eat,

156
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:26,620
but I think adding a
little color to our village

157
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:29,187
is good for making things
feel civilized.

158
00:07:29,318 --> 00:07:31,189
Outside of the farm work I do,

159
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,626
the villagers ask me to build

160
00:07:32,756 --> 00:07:35,455
all sorts of little
things for them.

161
00:07:35,585 --> 00:07:37,848
Thanks to the
almighty farming tool,

162
00:07:37,979 --> 00:07:39,676
I can make things for them

163
00:07:39,807 --> 00:07:42,897
even though I have no
experience in construction.

164
00:07:43,027 --> 00:07:44,768
I thank God for
these blessings.

165
00:07:44,899 --> 00:07:49,904
I also like to occasionally
join everyone

166
00:07:50,034 --> 00:07:51,775
for their battle training.

167
00:07:51,906 --> 00:07:54,561
[swords thudding]

168
00:07:54,691 --> 00:07:56,693
But Anne and the maids
strongly advised

169
00:07:56,824 --> 00:07:58,129
we hold regular training

170
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:00,610
just in case
anything should happen.

171
00:08:00,741 --> 00:08:02,830
Oh well, getting some
more exercise

172
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:04,396
is good for everyone's health.

173
00:08:04,527 --> 00:08:05,397
[woman grunts loudly]

174
00:08:05,528 --> 00:08:06,398
Huh?

175
00:08:06,529 --> 00:08:07,487
[women panting]

176
00:08:07,617 --> 00:08:09,314
- Okay, let's keep going!

177
00:08:09,445 --> 00:08:11,578
If we keep eating the way
we currently do

178
00:08:11,708 --> 00:08:13,493
in this well-stocked village,

179
00:08:13,623 --> 00:08:15,320
one day we'll no longer
be able to fit

180
00:08:15,451 --> 00:08:17,279
into our sacred maid uniforms!

181
00:08:17,409 --> 00:08:20,717
I think mine's already starting
to become a tighter fit!

182
00:08:20,848 --> 00:08:22,023
Let's go!

183
00:08:22,153 --> 00:08:24,155
- Maybe I need some
more exercise.

184
00:08:24,286 --> 00:08:26,723
[mysterious music]

185
00:08:28,116 --> 00:08:29,552
[Hiraku groans]

186
00:08:29,683 --> 00:08:34,775
[Hiraku grunting]
[sword thudding]

187
00:08:34,905 --> 00:08:36,603
I'm already at my limit.

188
00:08:36,733 --> 00:08:38,082
Huh?

189
00:08:38,213 --> 00:08:39,910
I bet I'd be better
with that one!

190
00:08:40,041 --> 00:08:41,129
Can I try it out?

191
00:08:41,259 --> 00:08:42,826
- Sure, that's fine by me.

192
00:08:42,957 --> 00:08:45,220
[Hiraku grunting]
[air whooshing]

193
00:08:45,350 --> 00:08:47,918
- This is harder than I thought.

194
00:08:48,049 --> 00:08:49,616
[daggers clang]
[Hiraku yelps]

195
00:08:49,746 --> 00:08:52,532
I guess I'm really not suited
to use normal weapons.

196
00:08:52,662 --> 00:08:54,882
But I still have this spear!

197
00:08:55,012 --> 00:08:56,579
[Hiraku grunts]
[air whooshes]

198
00:08:56,710 --> 00:08:57,885
[Ya yelps]

199
00:08:58,015 --> 00:08:59,277
[crowd howls]

200
00:08:59,408 --> 00:09:01,149
- That was so amazing!
How did you do that?

201
00:09:01,279 --> 00:09:04,065
- [Hiraku] I'm not exactly
sure when I can use this.

202
00:09:04,195 --> 00:09:06,023
Once the sun starts to set,

203
00:09:06,154 --> 00:09:08,635
I wrap up the work
I was doing and head home.

204
00:09:08,765 --> 00:09:11,202
Oh, I've never seen
this dish before.

205
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:13,944
- [giggles] This is a new
menu item we're trying out.

206
00:09:14,075 --> 00:09:15,380
It's simmered killer rabbit

207
00:09:15,511 --> 00:09:17,382
served with a sweet
buttery honey sauce.

208
00:09:17,513 --> 00:09:18,862
Please give it a try, sir.

209
00:09:18,993 --> 00:09:20,037
- How confident?

210
00:09:20,168 --> 00:09:21,473
- About 20%.

211
00:09:21,604 --> 00:09:23,040
- That's pretty low.

212
00:09:23,171 --> 00:09:24,346
- Super sweet!

213
00:09:24,476 --> 00:09:25,652
- I'd like you to
only present dishes

214
00:09:25,782 --> 00:09:27,784
that you have at least
50% confidence in.

215
00:09:27,915 --> 00:09:29,612
- I can not do that.

216
00:09:29,743 --> 00:09:32,093
We can not afford to waste
any of our food.

217
00:09:32,223 --> 00:09:33,660
- [Hiraku] Good point.

218
00:09:33,790 --> 00:09:35,444
[Hiraku grunts]

219
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:38,012
I did my best to enjoy the meal.

220
00:09:38,142 --> 00:09:39,840
[Hiraku chuckles]

221
00:09:39,970 --> 00:09:43,104
At dinner time, a lot more
people gather around the table.

222
00:09:43,234 --> 00:09:45,846
We report anything that
we want everyone to hear.

223
00:09:45,976 --> 00:09:49,719
- Mayor, Princess Yuri
has sent a letter to you.

224
00:09:49,850 --> 00:09:51,460
- Huh, wonder why?

225
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:53,157
Let's see,

226
00:09:53,288 --> 00:09:55,551
"I'd like to eat the apples
from your village again.

227
00:09:55,682 --> 00:09:58,423
"Also, I'd like a dress."
What is this?

228
00:09:58,554 --> 00:10:00,121
- She really liked the clothes

229
00:10:00,251 --> 00:10:02,776
that Zabuton made for her
while she was here,

230
00:10:02,906 --> 00:10:05,039
and was wondering if she
could have more made.

231
00:10:05,169 --> 00:10:06,083
- I see.

232
00:10:06,214 --> 00:10:07,650
- [Flowrem] I apologize.

233
00:10:07,781 --> 00:10:10,305
I'll tell her to stop making
so many requests of us.

234
00:10:10,435 --> 00:10:13,525
- Well, I'm sure Zabuton will
be happy to make something.

235
00:10:13,656 --> 00:10:15,484
[water trickling]

236
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:19,488
Once I've rested a bit after
dinner, it's bath time.

237
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:23,623
I pretty much have the men's
bathhouse all to myself.

238
00:10:23,753 --> 00:10:27,365
I couldn't really relax when
we only had one bathhouse.

239
00:10:27,496 --> 00:10:30,978
I'm really glad I forced them
to build a men's bathhouse.

240
00:10:31,108 --> 00:10:33,328
This is paradise.

241
00:10:33,458 --> 00:10:36,679
After I get out of the bath,
it's time to relax,

242
00:10:36,810 --> 00:10:40,596
or at least... I wish it was.

243
00:10:40,727 --> 00:10:43,730
This is usually where
I start to feel uneasy.

244
00:10:48,212 --> 00:10:49,953
- He's about to enter his house.

245
00:10:50,084 --> 00:10:52,434
- Right, I've got
eyes on him here.

246
00:10:52,564 --> 00:10:55,089
- He's headed
straight for his bedroom.

247
00:10:55,219 --> 00:10:56,438
- Understood.

248
00:10:56,568 --> 00:10:58,266
[Hiraku sighs]

249
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:02,574
- Why is it that I can still
feel their eyes on me

250
00:11:02,705 --> 00:11:05,447
even though I'm inside my room?

251
00:11:05,577 --> 00:11:07,928
Ah, someone help me!

252
00:11:08,058 --> 00:11:10,321
[doors thud]

253
00:11:10,452 --> 00:11:11,496
- [Leef] Our cover is blown!

254
00:11:11,627 --> 00:11:13,063
- [Lea] Everyone, retreat!

255
00:11:13,194 --> 00:11:14,499
- [Hiraku] I'm sure they're
just keeping watch

256
00:11:14,630 --> 00:11:16,414
because they want to
keep me safe.

257
00:11:16,545 --> 00:11:18,155
That's what I tell myself.

258
00:11:18,286 --> 00:11:19,548
[Hiraku groans]

259
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:22,812
Oh well, even with stuff
like that happening,

260
00:11:22,943 --> 00:11:26,120
I couldn't be happier with
my everyday life here.

261
00:11:26,250 --> 00:11:28,513
God, thank you once again

262
00:11:28,644 --> 00:11:31,386
for giving me a
second chance at life.

263
00:11:31,516 --> 00:11:33,910
I'll do my best again tomorrow.

264
00:11:34,041 --> 00:11:36,783
Oh yeah, I need to have
those hidden doors

265
00:11:36,913 --> 00:11:38,567
sealed up tomorrow too.

266
00:11:39,307 --> 00:11:40,308
Farming Life...

267
00:11:40,438 --> 00:11:41,265
- [Lu] ...In Another...

268
00:11:41,396 --> 00:11:43,441
- [Hiraku] ...World.

269
00:11:43,572 --> 00:11:46,749
Whether it's day or night
here in the village,

270
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:48,055
Donovan and the dwarves

271
00:11:48,185 --> 00:11:50,535
are always hard at work
making alcohol.

272
00:11:50,666 --> 00:11:52,189
When it comes to dwarves,

273
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,974
I used to imagine them
being merry,

274
00:11:54,104 --> 00:11:56,367
and getting drunk all the time.
[dwarves laughing]

275
00:11:56,498 --> 00:11:59,370
- There's no way we could
possibly produce good alcohol

276
00:11:59,501 --> 00:12:01,068
if we were drunk while working.

277
00:12:01,198 --> 00:12:02,765
- Indeed, you're right.

278
00:12:02,896 --> 00:12:05,463
Even the man in charge of
watching the fire would-

279
00:12:05,594 --> 00:12:08,466
- The man in charge of the fire
drinking on the job?

280
00:12:08,597 --> 00:12:10,642
Out of the question!
That could cause a fire!

281
00:12:10,773 --> 00:12:12,209
- Indeed, you're right.

282
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:15,691
As you can see, they take
their job very seriously.

283
00:12:15,822 --> 00:12:17,562
[Hiraku groans]

284
00:12:17,693 --> 00:12:19,477
- Do you think this is okay?

285
00:12:19,608 --> 00:12:22,045
- Nope, this one here
is no good.

286
00:12:22,176 --> 00:12:22,959
- [Hiraku] Huh?

287
00:12:23,090 --> 00:12:24,874
- It's lost it's flavor.

288
00:12:25,005 --> 00:12:27,485
This is bad booze that does
nothing but burn your throat.

289
00:12:27,616 --> 00:12:30,010
- So, are you gonna
throw it away?

290
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:33,622
- Nope, we've still got
uses for this.

291
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:35,276
We'll distill it some more,

292
00:12:35,406 --> 00:12:37,757
and then cut it with a variety
of different fruit juices.

293
00:12:37,887 --> 00:12:40,150
All right, back to
the drawing board.

294
00:12:40,281 --> 00:12:42,065
Let's rethink how
we're distilling it.

295
00:12:42,196 --> 00:12:44,024
- [Hiraku] I have nothing
but respect

296
00:12:44,154 --> 00:12:46,461
for the passion with which
they make alcohol.

297
00:12:46,591 --> 00:12:48,593
- [Donovan] Hey, Mayor!
- [Hiraku] Hmm?

298
00:12:48,724 --> 00:12:51,422
- Could you increase the amount
of grapes we're harvesting?

299
00:12:51,553 --> 00:12:53,468
I need three times
the current harvest.

300
00:12:53,598 --> 00:12:56,036
- [Hiraku] Oh, okay,
I'll see what I can do.

301
00:12:56,166 --> 00:12:59,474
Increase the harvest
three times?

302
00:12:59,604 --> 00:13:01,955
Three times, huh?

303
00:13:02,085 --> 00:13:04,087
Well, everyone here
really loves their wine.

304
00:13:04,218 --> 00:13:05,697
- [Sena] Mayor!
- Hmm?

305
00:13:05,828 --> 00:13:07,874
[Sena panting]
What is it?

306
00:13:08,004 --> 00:13:11,878
- Hmm, there's this
strange man that showed up.

307
00:13:12,617 --> 00:13:14,141
- A strange man?

308
00:13:14,271 --> 00:13:17,274
[dramatic music]

309
00:13:18,536 --> 00:13:20,234
It's a strange man?

310
00:13:20,364 --> 00:13:22,932
How did he even make it
this far in the first place?

311
00:13:23,063 --> 00:13:27,241
He got by Granmaria and
Zabuton without them noticing?

312
00:13:27,371 --> 00:13:29,634
- Oh, is that the Progenitor?

313
00:13:29,765 --> 00:13:31,898
- Lulucy!

314
00:13:32,028 --> 00:13:33,290
[Hiraku grunts]
[Lu giggles]

315
00:13:33,421 --> 00:13:35,727
- Ah, the Progenitor?

316
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:40,210
- [Flora] It's been
a long time, Progenitor.

317
00:13:40,341 --> 00:13:41,690
- You look quite well, Flora.

318
00:13:41,821 --> 00:13:43,170
- [Flora] I am.

319
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:45,346
- When I first heard that
Lulucy was with child,

320
00:13:45,476 --> 00:13:48,088
I was positive there must have
been some sort of mistake.

321
00:13:48,218 --> 00:13:50,003
It looks like I was wrong.

322
00:13:50,133 --> 00:13:52,701
- Yes, I'm quite
surprised myself.

323
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:55,399
- That's right,
we vampires usually tend

324
00:13:55,530 --> 00:13:56,966
to continue our bloodline

325
00:13:57,097 --> 00:13:59,882
by forming new bloodpacts,
though rarely [chuckles].

326
00:14:00,013 --> 00:14:02,363
But children are
a lovely treasure.

327
00:14:02,493 --> 00:14:03,930
You must take care of yours.

328
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:06,106
- Yes, I will, thank you.

329
00:14:06,236 --> 00:14:08,717
- What do you mean
he's the Progenitor?

330
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:10,632
- Ah, to put it simply,

331
00:14:10,762 --> 00:14:12,242
I guess you could say
that he would be

332
00:14:12,373 --> 00:14:14,070
the equivalent of
a grandfather.

333
00:14:14,201 --> 00:14:15,855
- Grandfather?

334
00:14:15,985 --> 00:14:18,901
- That's right,
I'm 4,000 years old now.

335
00:14:19,032 --> 00:14:20,207
- 4,000?

336
00:14:20,337 --> 00:14:22,035
- Well I sorta forget
the exact number.

337
00:14:22,165 --> 00:14:23,688
- [Hiraku] I can't see him
as anything

338
00:14:23,819 --> 00:14:26,082
other than a
regular young guy.

339
00:14:26,213 --> 00:14:27,823
- The trick to a long life

340
00:14:27,954 --> 00:14:29,912
is to occasionally
erase your memories.

341
00:14:30,043 --> 00:14:31,522
- Your memories?

342
00:14:31,653 --> 00:14:33,263
- [Vargryfe] I make sure to
keep the important stuff,

343
00:14:33,394 --> 00:14:35,309
like my name and
the clan I belong to,

344
00:14:35,439 --> 00:14:38,529
then I make everything else
go poof and forget about it.

345
00:14:38,660 --> 00:14:40,009
- It goes poof and gone?

346
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:41,532
Isn't that kind of scary?

347
00:14:41,663 --> 00:14:43,317
- It was a bit scary
the first time,

348
00:14:43,447 --> 00:14:45,493
but I got used to it
after that.

349
00:14:45,623 --> 00:14:48,191
It's been about 200 years
since last I did it,

350
00:14:48,322 --> 00:14:51,238
so I still feel pretty young
and vibrant now.

351
00:14:51,368 --> 00:14:54,154
- I didn't know vampires
had that sort of ability.

352
00:14:54,284 --> 00:14:56,721
- [Vargryfe] We don't,
I use magic for that.

353
00:14:56,852 --> 00:14:59,115
- Magic sounds really
useful to have.

354
00:14:59,246 --> 00:15:01,074
- Oh, by the way,

355
00:15:01,204 --> 00:15:03,903
I'm sorry I entered the village
without saying hello.

356
00:15:04,033 --> 00:15:06,906
I had planned to just have a
look around and then leave,

357
00:15:07,036 --> 00:15:09,778
but I was drawn in
by a certain presence.

358
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,171
- Presence?

359
00:15:11,301 --> 00:15:13,086
- That great statue
below the big tree!

360
00:15:13,216 --> 00:15:15,001
It is simply wonderful!

361
00:15:15,131 --> 00:15:17,742
It's truly a splendid likeness
of the great creator!

362
00:15:17,873 --> 00:15:19,962
Before I knew it, I was bowing.

363
00:15:20,093 --> 00:15:22,051
- Oh, that's what you meant.

364
00:15:22,182 --> 00:15:23,270
If you know his likeness,

365
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,054
does that mean
you've met God before?

366
00:15:25,185 --> 00:15:27,839
- [Vargryfe] Yes, just once,
when I was born.

367
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:29,276
He told me to do my best,

368
00:15:29,406 --> 00:15:31,060
even though I'd have
an abnormal body.

369
00:15:31,191 --> 00:15:33,889
- And by abnormal body
he meant vampire?

370
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:34,977
- I believe so.

371
00:15:35,108 --> 00:15:36,413
And thanks to that advice,

372
00:15:36,544 --> 00:15:38,372
I feel like I've faced
a lot of hardships

373
00:15:38,502 --> 00:15:40,417
and been saved
a number of times.

374
00:15:40,548 --> 00:15:42,680
But I can't be sure since
I've erased my memories!

375
00:15:42,811 --> 00:15:45,553
Oh well, I get the feeling
that I've done my best!

376
00:15:45,683 --> 00:15:47,598
[Vargryfe laughs nervously]
[Flora sighs]

377
00:15:47,729 --> 00:15:48,991
- Okay.

378
00:15:49,122 --> 00:15:51,820
- However, I do remember
the great creator.

379
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:55,084
It's just I'm afraid I can't
remember his exact appearance.

380
00:15:55,215 --> 00:15:56,956
Was he an old man?

381
00:15:57,086 --> 00:15:58,305
Or maybe a young man?

382
00:15:58,435 --> 00:15:59,959
What color were his eyes?

383
00:16:00,089 --> 00:16:01,743
What color was his hair?

384
00:16:01,873 --> 00:16:04,441
I've tried numerous times
to create a likeness of him,

385
00:16:04,572 --> 00:16:07,749
but I've never created
anything as real as that.

386
00:16:07,879 --> 00:16:10,447
I'm sure living nearby
a masterpiece like that,

387
00:16:10,578 --> 00:16:13,407
means that every single day
of your life is amazing!

388
00:16:13,537 --> 00:16:14,886
It must be so nice!

389
00:16:15,017 --> 00:16:17,411
I'm so jealous! Wow!

390
00:16:17,541 --> 00:16:19,587
- He wants it, right?
- [Lu] Mm-hmm.

391
00:16:19,717 --> 00:16:21,763
- Amazing, oh, so beautiful!
- Um, about that statue.

392
00:16:21,893 --> 00:16:23,721
It belongs to the village,

393
00:16:23,852 --> 00:16:25,810
so I don't think I can
offer it to you.

394
00:16:25,941 --> 00:16:26,855
[head thuds]

395
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,030
- I knew it.

396
00:16:28,161 --> 00:16:29,989
I get it, but it's too bad!

397
00:16:30,119 --> 00:16:31,773
Mm, too bad!

398
00:16:31,903 --> 00:16:33,514
I am reading the room
right, yeah?

399
00:16:33,644 --> 00:16:34,819
- [Hiraku] Uh-huh.

400
00:16:34,950 --> 00:16:36,473
[Flora and Lu whimpering]

401
00:16:36,604 --> 00:16:37,779
- Too bad.

402
00:16:37,909 --> 00:16:38,954
- If you'd like-
[Vargryfe groans]

403
00:16:39,085 --> 00:16:40,782
I could make you a new one.

404
00:16:40,912 --> 00:16:42,305
I'm not a sculptor,

405
00:16:42,436 --> 00:16:44,960
so I'm not sure if you'll
like what I make or not.

406
00:16:45,091 --> 00:16:46,135
- You mean it?

407
00:16:46,266 --> 00:16:47,615
I'd love that so much!

408
00:16:47,745 --> 00:16:49,182
I am so happy.

409
00:16:49,312 --> 00:16:50,531
Thank you, Mayor!

410
00:16:50,661 --> 00:16:52,185
[all chuckle]

411
00:16:54,143 --> 00:16:55,275
- [Hiraku] How do you like it?

412
00:16:55,405 --> 00:16:56,406
[dramatic music]

413
00:16:56,537 --> 00:16:58,017
- I think he likes it.

414
00:16:58,147 --> 00:16:59,453
- I think you're correct.

415
00:16:59,583 --> 00:17:01,716
- Sorry for the sudden request.

416
00:17:01,846 --> 00:17:03,979
How much should I
pay you for it?

417
00:17:04,110 --> 00:17:06,851
- Nothing, I can't take
money for this.

418
00:17:06,982 --> 00:17:09,898
God isn't something that you're
supposed to profit off of.

419
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:13,075
- I understand,
then I'll have to think about

420
00:17:13,206 --> 00:17:15,208
something else
I can do as thanks.

421
00:17:15,338 --> 00:17:17,775
Lu, make sure you give birth
to a healthy baby.

422
00:17:17,906 --> 00:17:19,299
- Yes.

423
00:17:19,429 --> 00:17:20,778
- [Vargryfe] Good health
to you too, Flora.

424
00:17:20,909 --> 00:17:22,302
- And you as well, Progenitor.

425
00:17:22,432 --> 00:17:26,088
- [chuckles] And Mayor,
thank you for everything.

426
00:17:26,219 --> 00:17:28,569
I'm grateful for this statue,

427
00:17:28,699 --> 00:17:30,875
and for what you've done for Lu.

428
00:17:31,006 --> 00:17:32,921
Keep taking care of her, okay?

429
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,270
- Yes.

430
00:17:34,401 --> 00:17:36,751
[Vargryfe humming]

431
00:17:36,881 --> 00:17:40,537
I was surprised at first,
but he's easygoing.

432
00:17:40,668 --> 00:17:42,365
- He sure is.

433
00:17:42,496 --> 00:17:44,889
- And to think, he's such an
incredibly high ranking person.

434
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:49,894
- Hmm, is he really
that important?

435
00:17:50,025 --> 00:17:51,896
- [Temple Master] Oh, my lord!

436
00:17:52,027 --> 00:17:52,680
[intense organ music]

437
00:17:52,810 --> 00:17:53,898
Welcome back.

438
00:17:54,029 --> 00:17:55,161
- It's been a while.

439
00:17:55,291 --> 00:17:56,640
How many years?

440
00:17:56,771 --> 00:17:59,426
- I believe it's been
50 years since last time.

441
00:17:59,556 --> 00:18:02,429
As you can see, I've lived long
enough to become an old man.

442
00:18:02,559 --> 00:18:05,519
- [Vargryfe] So you're in charge
of the temple now?

443
00:18:05,649 --> 00:18:07,738
- [Temple Master] Yes,
it's going on 30 years.

444
00:18:07,869 --> 00:18:10,480
- [Vargryfe] Well, you've always
been a devout believer.

445
00:18:10,611 --> 00:18:12,265
You're the man for the job.

446
00:18:12,395 --> 00:18:14,005
- [Temple Master]
Thank you very much.

447
00:18:14,136 --> 00:18:15,790
- [Vargryfe]
Has anything changed?

448
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,313
- Not a thing.

449
00:18:17,444 --> 00:18:19,881
Everything is as it
always was, My Lord.

450
00:18:20,011 --> 00:18:22,231
- I see, I'm rather glad
to hear that,

451
00:18:22,362 --> 00:18:24,842
but there's going to be a
big change starting today.

452
00:18:24,973 --> 00:18:26,757
- What might you mean
by that, My Lord?

453
00:18:26,888 --> 00:18:29,456
- I want to enshrine this
statue here in this temple.

454
00:18:29,586 --> 00:18:32,023
- [Temple Master] You do,
what kind of statue is that?

455
00:18:32,154 --> 00:18:33,982
- You'll just have to
wait and see.

456
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,027
I want you to put it in
the very best spot.

457
00:18:36,158 --> 00:18:38,465
- Hmm, well, if that's the case,

458
00:18:38,595 --> 00:18:41,076
then we would have to move out
the statue of the creator

459
00:18:41,207 --> 00:18:44,035
that was crafted by the
master sculptor, Toorook.

460
00:18:44,166 --> 00:18:46,821
But we can't move
the most beloved statue

461
00:18:46,951 --> 00:18:49,040
in this temple from
its resting place.

462
00:18:49,171 --> 00:18:50,955
- Yeah, of course we can.

463
00:18:51,086 --> 00:18:52,827
- Yes, sir.

464
00:18:53,741 --> 00:18:55,438
Oh...

465
00:18:55,569 --> 00:19:00,313
This is such a
majestic work of art.

466
00:19:00,443 --> 00:19:03,664
It must have been made by
quite a famous sculptor.

467
00:19:03,794 --> 00:19:06,797
We must be sure that everyone
properly honors their name.

468
00:19:06,928 --> 00:19:09,278
- I think it would be
better if we didn't.

469
00:19:09,409 --> 00:19:11,062
He doesn't strike me as the type

470
00:19:11,193 --> 00:19:13,456
to appreciate stuff like that.

471
00:19:13,587 --> 00:19:15,241
Besides, I'd rather not disturb

472
00:19:15,371 --> 00:19:17,068
the peaceful life he's built.

473
00:19:17,199 --> 00:19:19,332
- Hmm, that is most unfortunate.

474
00:19:19,462 --> 00:19:21,334
- Although, I think it's fine

475
00:19:21,464 --> 00:19:23,249
if we were to quietly
support him.

476
00:19:23,379 --> 00:19:24,685
- Right.

477
00:19:24,815 --> 00:19:26,339
- Let all the other temples
know immediately.

478
00:19:26,469 --> 00:19:28,384
Tell them to be
respectful of him,

479
00:19:28,515 --> 00:19:31,692
as well as respectful of
The Great Tree Village.

480
00:19:31,822 --> 00:19:33,607
- [Temple Master] Right away.

481
00:19:33,737 --> 00:19:34,869
[Hiraku sneezes]

482
00:19:34,999 --> 00:19:36,305
- Are you okay, Mayor?

483
00:19:36,436 --> 00:19:39,613
- Yeah, yeah, that just
caught me off guard.

484
00:19:39,743 --> 00:19:41,615
It's been a long time
since I've sneezed.

485
00:19:41,745 --> 00:19:42,659
[light piano music]

486
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:43,834
Huh?

487
00:19:43,965 --> 00:19:45,358
[light piano music]

488
00:19:45,488 --> 00:19:48,535
The Progenitor sent us
a magnificent piano.

489
00:19:48,665 --> 00:19:51,146
I refused to take
payment for the statue,

490
00:19:51,277 --> 00:19:53,192
so this was a gift
for Lu's pregnancy.

491
00:19:53,322 --> 00:19:57,805
He's really considerate
for someone so important.

492
00:19:57,935 --> 00:20:00,242
We talked for a while about
where we would put it.

493
00:20:00,373 --> 00:20:02,070
- [Daga] [groans] There we go.

494
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:04,855
- [Hiraku] We decided on
the village's dining hall.

495
00:20:04,986 --> 00:20:06,770
Thanks guys, good work.

496
00:20:06,901 --> 00:20:08,511
- [Daga] Good work, everyone.

497
00:20:08,642 --> 00:20:10,600
- The piano that was gifted.

498
00:20:10,731 --> 00:20:13,690
- Is it the kind you would find
only in a large temple?

499
00:20:13,821 --> 00:20:15,344
- Yeah, that's the kind of piano

500
00:20:15,475 --> 00:20:17,781
that only gets used
for big ceremonies.

501
00:20:17,912 --> 00:20:19,957
- Hey, guys, you think
we can play it?

502
00:20:20,088 --> 00:20:21,872
- This is a once,

503
00:20:22,003 --> 00:20:25,224
no, more like a never in a
lifetime chance to play one.

504
00:20:25,354 --> 00:20:29,140
- [Roaju] [sighs] That means
if we can play this piano now,

505
00:20:29,271 --> 00:20:32,187
we'll be able to brag about this
for the rest of our lives!

506
00:20:34,102 --> 00:20:35,669
[all sighing]

507
00:20:35,799 --> 00:20:37,236
- You can go first, Roaju.

508
00:20:37,366 --> 00:20:38,454
- Huh?

509
00:20:38,585 --> 00:20:40,108
- I'm fine with
playing later too.

510
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:41,327
[Roaju yelps]

511
00:20:41,457 --> 00:20:44,199
[all sigh]

512
00:20:44,330 --> 00:20:47,811
This thing is way too scary
for us to even try playing!

513
00:20:47,942 --> 00:20:49,683
- My hands are sweating so much!

514
00:20:49,813 --> 00:20:52,381
- If we break it, that will be
the end of our short lives!

515
00:20:52,512 --> 00:20:55,384
- Huh, you want another piano?

516
00:20:55,515 --> 00:20:58,126
- For, for us to practice on.
- Please, Mayor?

517
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:00,911
We don't mind if it's old and
raggedy and beat up badly.

518
00:21:01,042 --> 00:21:03,392
- Actually, an old piano
would be for the best.

519
00:21:03,523 --> 00:21:05,742
- Can't you play
the one we have?

520
00:21:05,873 --> 00:21:07,744
- [Girls] No, we can't do it!

521
00:21:07,875 --> 00:21:11,095
- What, huh, why are you crying?

522
00:21:11,226 --> 00:21:12,706
We talked to Michael,

523
00:21:12,836 --> 00:21:15,404
and had him procure
a practice piano for us.

524
00:21:17,145 --> 00:21:18,538
Hmm...

525
00:21:18,668 --> 00:21:21,280
I don't really know
anything about these,

526
00:21:21,410 --> 00:21:24,544
but the one we got from the
Progenitor seems a lot fancier.

527
00:21:24,674 --> 00:21:27,808
Now I feel bad that he sent us
something so nice.

528
00:21:27,938 --> 00:21:31,942
[upbeat piano music]

529
00:21:32,073 --> 00:21:33,466
The pianos were a hit.

530
00:21:33,596 --> 00:21:35,294
Everyone wanted to play.

531
00:21:36,643 --> 00:21:38,471
The only ones who
could already play

532
00:21:38,601 --> 00:21:42,083
were Flowrem and the girls
from the Demonic Kingdom,

533
00:21:42,213 --> 00:21:46,348
but everyone else seems to enjoy
practicing to get better.

534
00:21:46,479 --> 00:21:49,656
[upbeat piano music]

535
00:22:06,412 --> 00:22:10,111
[intense piano music]

536
00:22:10,241 --> 00:22:12,113
[groans]

537
00:22:12,243 --> 00:22:14,724
I just wish they'd stop
playing at night.

538
00:22:14,855 --> 00:22:18,380
[intense piano music]

539
00:22:18,511 --> 00:22:21,818
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

540
00:23:47,556 --> 00:23:51,734
[rustic music playing]

